<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammad Ali Khan Zand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammad Ali Khan Zand was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a>, the founder of the Zand state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. After his father's death in 1779 his uncle Zaki Khan proclaimed him and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-fath-khan-zand">Abu al-Fath Khan</a> joint rulers while holding real power himself. The young princes were soon pushed aside, and the succession disputes among the Zand family opened fifteen years of civil war.</p></div>
